# 12. INVENTORY VALUE AND NUMERIC CALCULATIONS

Implement the following calculations accurately.

### Individual product value

Product Value = Unit Price × Quantity

### Total inventory value

Total Inventory Value = Sum of Product Value for all products

### Total units

Total Units = Sum of Current Stock Quantity

### Low-stock inventory value

Calculate the total inventory value of products classified as low-stock.

### Out-of-stock inventory value

This should normally be zero because those products have no remaining units.

### Category valuation

Calculate total inventory value for each category.

### Stock summary

Calculate the number of products in each stock status.

Use Python numeric operations and functions for these calculations.

Keep calculations in the backend rather than hardcoding numbers in the interface.

Use consistent Indian Rupee formatting.

